<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Nervii</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 57 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The fiercest of the Belgic peoples, who banned wine and luxuries and almost defeated Caesar at the Battle of the Sabis in 57 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Nervii lived in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/county-of-hainaut">Hainaut</a> region of modern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-belgium">Belgium</a> and northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scheldt">Scheldt</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sambre">Sambre</a>. Caesar reports that they forbade merchants and wine, believing luxuries weakened courage, and that they were proud of their Germanic descent.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They had no cavalry to speak of and fought on foot, using thick hedges of bent saplings to block their land against raiders. Their war leader in 57 BCE was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boduognatus">Boduognatus</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>At the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-sabis">Sabis</a> (probably the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sambre">Sambre</a>) in 57 BCE they surprised Caesar's camp and were crushed only after a desperate battle. In 54 BCE they besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quintus-tullius-cicero">Quintus Cicero</a>'s winter camp. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> their chief town was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavay">Bagacum</a> (Bavay), later <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/prince-bishopric-of-cambrai">Cambrai</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/nervii.jpg" alt="Nervii" width="320" height="234"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gaule_Belgique.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 57 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Boduognatus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/belgium">Belgium</a>, <a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-178&amp;focus=nervii" aria-label="Nervii on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4760 424 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Nervii lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5080 680L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5080 680h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5080 680h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=-178&amp;focus=nervii">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

